  <!-- bic:source=blank -->
  # Hooks Lab configuration snapshot v4 - tool-scoped demos and limited prompt edits

  Use for configuration Q&A. This is an authored snapshot, not an API for inspecting later portal edits.
  Do not claim a hook ran just because it is configured. Distinguish live evidence, synthetic workflow
  tests, and source contracts. This sample targets the six event types in the production UX screenshot
  provided on 2026-10-23, not every event present in the CLI object model. Explain observed results
  without inventing trace access or revealing hidden reasoning.

  ## Explain it simply

  For an ordinary "Show my hooks" request, give a short hook / prompt / expected result overview
  using the demo guide. Do not show the implementation table or IDs below unless asked for technical
  details. Describe hooks as steps that can change what happens at a particular moment.
  The learner copies a demo prompt; the agent supplies the tool inputs.
  Start adds the note "The user is really interested in learning more about hooks."
  That is sample-provided context, not a personal fact inferred from outside information.
  User prompt submitted changes only demo-secret, demo-pin and demo-password to [redacted], leaving
  the rest of the request intact. These are sample words, not real secrets.
  Error is a walkthrough using made-up examples, not a live system failure.

  ## Implementation reference - details on request

  Model: Auto. Built-in web search: enabled, without hook bindings. Seven maker-configured tools use MSN Weather
  shared_msnweather / CurrentWeather, Invoker authentication, connection reference
  new_sharedmsnweather_093bc. The connector requires Location and units (C metric or I imperial);
  the verified runtime exposes current_weather_location and current_weather_units instead.
  weather_live has no tool hooks. Dedicated aliases select rewrite, deny, replace, augment, suppress
  and intentional failure demos.
  The aliases are distinct tool components, not extra unsupported connector arguments. The demo guide
  maps maker display names to the actual generated runtime names. weather_rewrite_demo was exposed
  as current_weather; others used current_weather_cr_hookslabtoolWeather<Scenario>_Hl<N>.
  That is historical naming evidence, not a guarantee after adding a component. Resolve the dedicated
  failure tool by its current catalog description or WeatherFailure_Hl7 identity; never use weather_live.

  | Hook component | Production UX event (native event) | Workflow name | Workflow ID | Scope |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | Start (pre-loop) - session context | Start (pre-loop) (SessionStart) | Hooks Lab - Session start | aeaca24c-d2ce-f111-a05d-0022480b1af1 | Session initialization |
  | User prompt submitted - prompt rewrite | User prompt submitted (UserPromptSubmitted) | Hooks Lab - Prompt rewrite | 416cee55-d2ce-f111-a05d-0022480b1af1 | Every prompt; only three exact demo strings change |
  | Pre tool use - weather | Pre tool use (PreTool) | Hooks Lab - Weather pre tool | 7d9cec7c-d2ce-f111-a05d-0022480b1af1 | WeatherRewrite_Hl2 and WeatherDeny_Hl3 only |
  | Post tool use - weather | Post tool use (PostTool) | Hooks Lab - Weather post tool | bd31f083-d2ce-f111-a05d-0022480b1af1 | WeatherReplace_Hl4, WeatherAugment_Hl5 and WeatherSuppress_Hl6 only |
  | After tool failure - failure context | After tool failure (PostToolFailure) | Hooks Lab - Tool failure | b0df4f5c-d2ce-f111-a05d-0022480b1af1 | WeatherFailure_Hl7 only |
  | Error - bounded recovery | Error (Error) | Hooks Lab - SDK error | eae04f5c-d2ce-f111-a05d-0022480b1af1 | SDK/model errors |

  Six hook components cover exactly six production UX event types, one binding per type.
  Every action is WorkflowHookAction. These workflows are hook actions, not ordinary callable tools.
  All three tool hooks have nonempty filteredTools using the exact component schema names
  cr_hookslab.tool.<component identity from the table>. No tool appears in more than one tool filter.
  WeatherLive_Hl1, skill loading and built-in tools have no tool-hook bindings.
  The two former built-in hook bindings were removed; their existing workflows are retained unbound.
  Workflow conditions are not hook-binding filters: a wildcard workflow that returns no changes
  still ran. This version removes that extra execution rather than merely returning a no-op.
  Component-based filters cannot individually select unregistered SDK built-ins such as bash,
  so the bash/web hook demos are intentionally removed rather than silently broken.

  Start and User prompt submitted are lifecycle events, not tool-scoped events. A first-turn
  "Demo weather deny" can therefore show User prompt submitted, Start, and one weather Pre tool
  use invocation. Loading the guide must not add Pre/Post tool entries. The denial must not invoke
  the removed built-in hook, a weather Post tool hook, or the failure-demo hook.

  ## Timing and effect
  - Start (pre-loop) / SessionStart adds the learning-interest note, with an internal HOOKLAB_SESSION_V1 marker.
    Quote the friendly note, not the marker, in ordinary replies. It cannot deny admission or directly
    send a greeting. Ordinary follow-up turns should not be described as new sessions.
  - User prompt submitted / UserPromptSubmitted replaces every occurrence of the exact lowercase strings
    demo-secret, demo-pin and demo-password with [redacted] through modifiedPrompt. It preserves all other
    text and does not disable tools, replace the entire request with instructions, or inspect earlier tool calls.
    Without a matching string it returns an empty modifiedPrompt, meaning no change. Matching is case-sensitive.
    The original message and workflow history can still contain the original text; this is not secure secret
    removal. This is not a blocking gate; additionalContext has a CLI no-op caveat.
  - Pre tool use / PreTool can deny a call, add context or replace its full argument object. A weather rewrite removes
    HOOKLAB_REWRITE: from the actual location field and forces the units field to C; other fields survive.
    The workflow recognizes the verified runtime names/keys as well as the maker names/connector keys.
    The UX describes allow, deny and confirmation, but this sample has verified deny, not allow/ask.
    Never present allow/ask as tested or as bypasses for platform consent or security.
  - Post tool use / PostTool runs after a tool executes. The UX describes successful or failed execution;
    this sample verified result replacement and augmentation on successful calls. Do not infer failure
    behavior from that coverage. modifiedResult replaces the result before the model consumes it.
    The required shape is {"textResultForLlm":"...","resultType":"success","toolTelemetry":{}}.
    Arbitrary JSON is not enough. additionalContext instead preserves the original result and augments it.
    Never attach inherited citations to synthetic replacement content.
  - suppressOutput is an SDK/channel visibility request, not proven redaction or a security boundary.
    Do not promise it hides information from the model or every client.
  - After tool failure / PostToolFailure is configured to add context to genuine failed tool events.
    It does not retry or convert failure to success. A deliberate weather-connector 404 triggered it
    and delivered HOOKLAB_FAILURE_CONTEXT. A bash nonzero exit did not trigger it in the observed
    preview; a command exit code and a runtime tool-failure event are not necessarily equivalent.
  - Error requests retry with retryCount 1 when recoverable, abort otherwise. The exact synthetic
    HOOKLAB_SYNTHETIC_SKIP error exercises skip in workflow contract tests only. Notification is generic
    and does not echo raw error data. Do not induce platform outages to demonstrate this.

  There is no supported outgoing/final-response interception hook in this sample. Post tool use result
  replacement does not overwrite messages already sent. No AgentStop, SessionEnd or OnSignIn demo is
  configured. This CLI has no AgentHook FailureMode setting; do not promise fail-closed hook execution.
  Host governance still applies to modified arguments. Prompts and hooks do not bypass authorization.

  ## Prior behavior evidence and current scope
  The following saved-draft checks established the hook effects before the tool-binding cleanup.
  They are not proof of invocation counts under the new filters; inspect current runs for that.
  - Start (pre-loop): workflow invocation confirmed. User prompt submitted: the earlier whole-prompt replacement
    was observed; that historical result does not establish the new limited-redaction behavior.
  - Pre tool use: weather rewriting and denial observed. The former built-in demos also worked but
    are no longer configured, because their wildcard hooks cluttered unrelated tool traces.
  - Post tool use: weather replacement and augmentation observed. Synthetic output was labeled.
  - suppressOutput: the workflow request was made, but data still reached the model. Client-side hiding
    was not verified; this is not redaction.
  - Error: synthetic workflow outputs verified retry/1, abort/0 and skip/0; no live SDK error was induced.
  - After tool failure: the connector-error behavior was live-verified using the impossible location
    HOOKLAB_FAIL_NOT_A_REAL_PLACE_8H6E. Connector 404 remained a failure, with added context and no retry.
    Workflow run 08584088474251052581667746995CU16 succeeded; its Explain_Controlled_Failure action
    returned HOOKLAB_FAILURE_CONTEXT. That earlier test used weather_live with a wildcard failure
    binding. This version uses only weather_failure_demo with a specific binding instead.
    The harmless bash exit-7 command did not invoke this hook.
  - These observations are saved-draft previews, not published-agent verification. AgentStop is not an
    outstanding demo: it was removed to match the six production UX event types.

  For examples, load hooks-demo-guide. If any tool or hook is unavailable, report the limitation;
  never fabricate a successful demonstration.
